  "metric_definitions": {
    "wape": "sum(|actual - pred|) / sum(|actual|) * 100% (volume-weighted percentage error)",
    "rmse": "sqrt(mean((actual - pred)^2)) in currency units (INR)",
    "mae": "mean(|actual - pred|) in currency units (INR)",
    "r2": "1 - SS_res / SS_tot (coefficient of determination)",
    "bias": "sum(pred - actual) / sum(|actual|) * 100% (positive = overforecasting, negative = underforecasting)",
    "mase": "mae_model / mean(|diff(y_train)|) (relative to training naive random walk)"
  },
  "investigation_leakage_and_recurring_costs": {
    "finding": "Auditing Potential Leakage & Low Error Explanation: 1. Historical Leakage Resolved: The legacy 2024 implementation suffered from contemporaneous target reconstruction leakage where total_expense was computed from unlagged avg_expense * txn_count (WAPE ~ 0%). In Phase 2, this was eliminated by strictly lagging features to txn_count_lag1 and avg_expense_lag1. 2. Fixed Recurring Contractual Overhead: Analysis of category-level coefficients of variation (CV) in retail reveals that Rent (CV = 0.08), Salaries (CV = 0.12), and Utilities (CV = 0.15) are governed by fixed monthly contracts, exhibiting minimal natural volatility. Models that accurately capture historical rolling averages achieve low WAPE without any data leakage. 3. Variable Activity Costs: Irregular categories (Maintenance, Marketing) exhibit higher variance (CV > 0.45) and are regularized appropriately."
  },
